  (rectangle (start 20.32 207.01) (end 166.37 355.6) (stroke (width 0.35) (type default)) (fill (type color) (color 214 92 64 0.10)) (uuid 79376e2a-baa8-408b-a49d-027300e18bcd))
  (text "3. HOT-SIDE SUPPLY (LNK3204 HALF-WAVE BUCK, 5 V, THEN 3.3 V)" (at 21.5900 208.2800 0) (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8) bold) (justify left top)) (uuid c2990774-3e36-4de5-bb7c-aebf0ca364e2))
  (text "Replaces the KP3310 (R1 study, hardware/sim/R1-study.md): half-wave charging through a surge resistor could not supply the 8-15 mA load.\nHigh-side buck referenced to L_BUS. RF 47R + 2 x M7 + pi filter (2 x 4.7 uF 450 V, 1 mH): simulated bulk/drain peak 465 V at a 4 kV surge\n(switch rated 725 V).\nFeedback: C25 samples Vout during freewheel; 2.00 V x (1 + 3.09k/2.49k) = 4.48 V + about 0.5 V diode offset = 5.0 V (trim R35 at bring-up).\nBP/M = 1 uF selects the reduced current limit (enough for 20 mA, allows a small choke). D9 must be <= 35 ns trr (enclosure above 70 C)." (at 21.5900 212.0900 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 0814572e-cb15-46f9-9c66-b0a65b3507e8))
