  (rectangle (start 179.07 199.39) (end 382.27 316.23) (stroke (width 0.35) (type default)) (fill (type color) (color 214 92 64 0.10)) (uuid 7328b134-8f54-4d7c-ab17-ed28a9d0cedf))
  (text "5. POLARITY AND EARTH CHECK (PULSE-WIDTH RATIO, S2 SCHEME F)" (at 180.3400 200.6600 0) (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8) bold) (justify left top)) (uuid eab10324-d6c3-4ad7-9181-b75f033dd08a))
  (text "Arm A: E -> 2 x 2M (HV) -> sense 47k -> L_BUS.  Arm B: E -> 2 x 2M (HV) + 47k -> N_F, so a missing earth floats to mid-supply.\nD3 (low leakage) passes the positive half-wave to R21; U4 compares it with 1.490 V (A) and 0.496 V (B). POL_A/POL_B are 50 Hz pulses.\nFirmware: duty d -> amplitude (TH/g + Vf)/cos(pi d), divided by the BL0939 mains peak, ratio to the unit's end-of-line k0:\n> 0.68 earthed and correct, 0.33-0.68 no earth (advisory, outlets empty only), < 0.33 swapped (outlets stay off). Run with relays open.\nEach arm must withstand a 6 kV impulse: VR37-class HV resistors." (at 180.3400 204.4700 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 6215331d-f230-4c55-bde4-1bb22666c6e6))
